course: dictionary
lesson: 2166
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «COVID-19 is caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus, first found in 2019» is about one particular virus, not the whole family.
explain: Look for clues. The words «the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus» point to one specific virus, and «first found in 2019» tells you when it was discovered. A family of viruses could not be "first found" in one year in that way.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. Try "the virus that caused COVID-19" in place of "coronavirus": it still makes sense. Then try "the family of viruses": it does not fit, so the sentence means one specific virus.
fact: A coronavirus is a type of virus, and the word can name a whole family of viruses.
fact: Under a microscope, coronaviruses have spikes that look like a crown.
fact: Some coronaviruses cause a common cold, and others cause more serious illnesses.
fact: In everyday talk, «coronavirus» can mean the virus that caused the COVID-19 pandemic, which spread around the world from 2020.
fact: People often say «Covid» for short, and it means the same illness.
exercise: «COVID-19 is caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus, first found in 2019.» In this sentence, what does coronavirus mean? | *One specific virus that causes COVID-19 | A hospital bed | A crown worn by a king | A family of viruses that includes colds
exercise: Under a microscope, what do the spikes on a coronavirus look like? | A star | A ladder | A wheel | *A crown
exercise: What do people often say for short when they mean COVID-19? | Pandemic | Corona | *Covid | Virus
test: The example sentence says that in most children COVID-19 is what? | Only found in animals | *Mild | Always very serious | Never caught
test: What can coronaviruses cause, according to the entry? | Only sunburn | *Illnesses from a common cold to serious illnesses | Only broken bones | Only toothache
exam: Which sentence uses coronavirus to mean the whole family of viruses? | *«Coronaviruses can cause illnesses from a common cold to serious ones.» | «The coronavirus was first found in 2019.» | «The coronavirus is caused by a crown.» | «The coronavirus made everyone stay at home.»
